content.thinking:
Step C: still only traversee red (17/1). The guard didn't break anything. Now **step D — D4: swept detection (slab method)**. I replace the positional-only `faceByDepth` entry in resolveBricks with `sweptHit` which:
- returns null if the segment doesn't intersect the expanded slab
- positional (tClose ≤ 0) → faceByDepth
- crossing (tClose > 0) → face by entry time
- then the flip + pushOut logic stays.

Note: for the swept crossing, pushOut needs the FACE ('bottom' for the traversee case → y = brick.y + h + r = 127). Then the ball is placed below the brick and vy flipped. Let me also make sure the pushed position for swept crossings doesn't break the other cases — the other cases are positional (tClose ≤ 0) → faceByDepth as before.

Implementation of sweptHit:

```js
// Swept AABB test (slab method): does the segment (px,py) -> (x,y) intersect
// the brick grown by the ball radius? Positional overlaps (the segment starts
// inside the box) resolve by penetration depth; crossings during the step
// resolve by the face entered last. Returns null when the segment misses.
function sweptHit(ball, brick) {
  const { px, py } = ball;
  const dx = ball.x - px;
  const dy = ball.y - py;

  const x0 = brick.x - ball.r;
  const x1 = brick.x + brick.w + ball.r;
  const y0 = brick.y - ball.r;
  const y1 = brick.y + brick.h + ball.r;

  let txIn, txOut;
  if (dx === 0) {
    if (px < x0 || px > x1) return null;
    txIn = -Infinity;
    txOut = Infinity;
  } else {
    txIn = Math.min((x0 - px) / dx, (x1 - px) / dx);
    txOut = Math.max((x0 - px) / dx, (x1 - px) / dx);
  }

  let tyIn, tyOut;
  if (dy === 0) {
    if (py < y0 || py > y1) return null;
    tyIn = -Infinity;
    tyOut = Infinity;
  } else {
    tyIn = Math.min((y0 - py) / dy, (y1 - py) / dy);
    tyOut = Math.max((y0 - py) / dy, (y1 - py) / dy);
